model {
  extend basalt.deployment {
    metadata {
      constraint "A deploy-time command whose outcome a resource reads is keyed on what it reads and carries no attempt identity: the source namespace, pool size, migration and pool database commands on every stage. A plan cannot know the outcome of a command that runs on every plan, so every resource waiting on one would plan as an update forever. The migration's key is the sources its imports reach, the hosted apps and the workspace packages, and the lockfile. A file that preparation rewrites for every revision and the migration does not import stays out of that key, and a check names every file preparation writes into it. The site build's key is every file the tree does not ignore and the lockfile, without the files that preparation rewrites for every revision, which no page or site script imports: otherwise the site, and every Worker that serves it, would change on every release. These commands therefore run only when their inputs change. A check that must run on every release reads no resource and belongs to the release entry, before apply. The pool size command names its stage, and its script refuses, before any provider call, a database or branch that is not that stage's own: a disposable test stage owns the one database and the two branches named after it, and every other stage owns only the main branch of a database that is not a test stage's."
    }
  }
}
